      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WITCH OF NOVA (2) stalked the lead and fought on well to finish 2.25 lengths away in third (25.75) at Shepparton in a Grade 5 over 450m. The form out of her last race has been franked. Key chance in this line up. JUNEAU SANGRIA (7) had been in super honest form hitting the frame four times on end before finishing fourth (25.74) at Warrnambool last time. Solid record here winning two races. Shapes as one to consider. ZIPPING SMEE (3) showed little early speed at his last couple, the latest finishing fifth (27.77) in a Grade 5 at this track. Yet to win out of this box but has been in the placings three times from six starts. A forward showing wouldn't surprise. LORIMER STREET (1) can sneak into the finish with the right run.",
